title: Scoped reconcile
tags: [[Reconcile]]
kind: reference
summary: A reconcile of one metarecord's subtree creates and refreshes there, but does no fingerprint or similarity matching.

A reconcile with `{"metarecord": "<uuid>"}` (`mf reconcile --metarecord <uuid>`,
`metarecord:reconcile`) runs on the subtree rooted at that metarecord — typically right
after setting `mf_watch = true` on a directory:

* walks it on disk (or refreshes the one file), evaluates eligibility for each path, creates the missing metarecords with all their `mfr_*` fields, and creates missing parent directories if needed;
* refreshes the stat fields of those already there (unless `refresh: false`), and fills in MIME types and embedded metadata;
* does ''no'' fingerprint or similarity matching — no orphan is followed. For that, reconcile the whole repository.

Its result always has `moved = 0` and no candidates. It fails — the task ends `failed` —
for an unknown metarecord, or one without a valid `mfr_path` (`nothing` or none).
